==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hverr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hweraz}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/xʷɛːr/|lang=is}}
* {{IPA|/kʰvɛːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛːr|lang=is}}

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m|hvers|hverir|pl2=hverar}}

# a [[hot spring]]{{jump|hot spring|s}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s2|hv|e|r|}}
Previously also declined according to the first declension, with plural ''hverar'':
{{is-decl-noun-m-s1|hv|e|r}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|goshver}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|is|lind}}
* {{l|is|heitur pottur}}
* {{l|is|pottur}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|hot spring}} {{l|is|laug}}, {{l|is|heit laug}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hverr|lang=non}} (from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hwarjaz}}) and {{m|non|*hver}} (from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hwaz}}), which were conflated in (late) Old Norse. Most of the inflected forms of *''hwaz'' have since become obsolete, and what remains in form is essentially the descendant of *''hwarjaz'', but with an extra form for the neuter nominative and accusative singular: ''hvað'' from Old Norse {{term|hvat|lang=non}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|is|hvur}}, {{l|is|hvör}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/xʷɛːr/|lang=is}}
* {{IPA|/kʰvɛːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛːr|lang=is}}
* {{IPA|/kʰv(ʏ~œ)ːr/|lang=is}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|is|pronoun|feminine|hver|neuter|hvert|or|hvað}}

# {{context|interrogative|lang=is}} [[who]], [[what]]
#: '''''Hver''' er ég?''
#:: '''Who''' am I?
#: '''''Hver''' [[stela|stal]] [[kaka#Icelandic|kökunni]] úr krúsinni í gær?''
#:: '''Who''' stole the cookie from the jar last night?
# {{context|interrogative|lang=is}} [[which]] (referring to one or several of more than two things or persons; may be qualified by a noun phrase in genitive or a noun phrase with the preposition {{term|af||of|lang=is}})
# {{context|interrogative|neuter singular|lang=is}} [[what]], which part (referring to part of a mass or group of things or people considered collectively; may be qualified by a noun phrase with the preposition {{term|af||of|lang=is}})
# {{context|relative|lang=is}} [[whichever]] (of more than two things or persons; followed by a relative clause; may be qualified by a noun phrase in genitive or a noun phrase with the preposition {{term|af||of|lang=is}})
# {{context|relative|neuter singular|lang=is}} [[whatever]] (followed by a relative clause; may be qualified by a noun phrase with the preposition {{term|af||of|lang=is}})
# {{context|relative|chiefly|archaic|lang=is}} [[who]], [[which]], [[that]] (used in the forming of relative clauses)
# {{context|indefinite|lang=is}} [[each]], [[every]]
#* ''Article 1'', [[Universal Declaration of Human Rights]] ([http://www.ohchr.org/EN/UDHR/Pages/Language.aspx?LangID=ice Icelandic], [http://www.ohchr.org/EN/UDHR/Pages/Language.aspx?LangID=eng English])
#*: '''''Hver''' maður er borinn frjáls og jafn öðrum að virðingu og réttindum. Menn eru gæddir vitsmunum og samvizku, og ber þeim að breyta bróðurlega hverjum við annan.''
#*:: '''All''' human beings are born free and equal in dignity and rights. They are endowed with reason and conscience and should act towards one another in a spirit of brotherhood.

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-pron-hver}}
The neuter form ''hvað'' is used with senses 1 and 3, ''hvert'' with others.

=====Derived terms=====
* [[hvers konar]]? (how? what kind of?)
* [[hvers vegna]]? ([[why]]?)
* [[hver sem er]] ([[whoever]])
* [[annar hver]] (every other one)
* [[hver af öðrum]]/[[hver eftir annan]] (one after the other)
* [[eins og hver annar]] (like everybody else)
* [[af hverju]]
* [[sinn er siður í landi hverju]]
* [[ber er hver að baki, nema sér bróður eigi]]
* [[leika við hvern sinn fingur]]
* [[hæla á hvert reipi]]

